.TH NOSTR-HOME-SYNCD 8 "2026-09-25" "nostr-homed 0.3" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
nostr-home-syncd \- user-scoped portable-home sync daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nostr-home-syncd
[\fB\-\-check\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nostr-home-syncd
is the user-scoped background daemon that watches
.I $HOME
via inotify, chunks and encrypts changed files, uploads them to the
configured Blossom servers, and republishes the kind-30078 pointer when
the batch closes. It always runs as the login user under
.B systemd \-\-user
via
.IR nostr-home-sync.service ;
running as root is a bug.
.PP
The daemon takes no command-line configuration beyond the
.B \-\-check
dry-run switch. Everything else is provided through environment variables
in the user unit file. Secret material is delivered to the daemon via a
per-session broker seed drop, described in
.B FILES
below.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Exercise the lock, interlock, and ignore-list stacks; report status; exit.
No network traffic, no snapshot, no publish. Safe to run alongside a live
daemon (subject to the lock).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Required (unless
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_TEST_MODE
is set, see below):
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_NSEC_HEX
64-hex secp256k1 signer for the kind-30078 pointer.
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_BLOSSOM
Comma-separated list of https:// Blossom server URLs.
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_RELAYS
Comma-separated list of wss:// relay URLs.
.PP
Optional:
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_D_TAG
Pointer d-tag override. Default:
.IR nostr-homed.home.v1:personal .
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_MIN_REPLICATION
Minimum Blossom replication before publishing. Default 2. The legacy name
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_MIN_REPL
is accepted for backwards compatibility.
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_STATE_DIR
Override the state directory. Default:
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/nostr-homed .
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_HOME
Override
.I $HOME
(tests only).
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_RESCAN_INTERVAL_SEC
Periodic full-tree rescan tick. 0 or unset disables. Non-zero closes
inotify
.B IN_Q_OVERFLOW
and add-watch race gaps.
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_SEED_FILE
Override the broker seed drop path. Default:
.IR /run/nostr-auth/session/<uid>/home_seed .
Read-once, unlinked, mlocked.
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_TEST_MODE
When set to 1, permits the (otherwise disabled)
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_SEED_HEX
env fallback so tests can seed home_key without a broker drop. MUST be off
in production.
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_SEED_HEX
64-hex seed for home_key derivation. Consulted only when TEST_MODE=1.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/nostr-auth/session/<uid>/home_seed
Broker seed drop, mode 0400, owned by the target uid. The daemon reads it
once, unlinks it, and holds the derived home_key in mlocked memory for the
process lifetime.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/nostr-homed/sync.lock
flock() sentinel that prevents two daemons for the same home from running
concurrently. A collision is not an error: the second instance exits 0.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/nostr-homed/porthome-status.json
Status file; kept up to date by the daemon.
.TP
.I ~/.nostr-home-limited
If present, the daemon refuses to start (\(dqlimited mode\(dq). Used by
admins to disable per-user sync without editing unit files.
.SH EXIT CODES
.RS
.TP 4
.B 0
Clean shutdown, or another instance already holds the sync.lock.
.TP 4
.B 2
Configuration failure (missing NSEC, missing Blossom, missing relays).
.TP 4
.B 3
Refused to run \(em
.I ~/.nostr-home-limited
present.
.TP 4
.B 4
Refused to run \(em NOSTR_HOME_STATE=partial in the environment.
.TP 4
.B 5
Failed to acquire sync.lock for reasons other than contention.
.RE
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Clean shutdown \(em finish the in-flight batch, publish (or roll back)
the pointer, release the lock, exit 0.
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Re-read the per-user quota override written by
.BR nostr-home-status (1)
.BR quota .
.SH SECURITY
Runs as the login user with the systemd
.B User=
directive; never gains capabilities; state and secrets are constrained to
.IR $HOME " and " /run/nostr-auth/session/<uid>/ .
Sets
.B RLIMIT_CORE
to 0. Wipes home_key on exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nostr-homed-provision (1),
.BR nostr-home-status (1),
.BR nostr-home-fuse (8),
.BR systemctl (1)
